# Corpus specimens are not redistributed here.
#
# The analysis in FORMAT-NOTES.md was performed on freely distributed .sbsar files
# (ambientCG, CC0) and .sbs sources published by their authors on GitHub under MIT,
# CC0 and MPL licences. Those files belong to their authors and are not republished
# in this repository. The tools reproduce every result from a local corpus.
corpus/
acg2/
new_acg/
new_sbs/
pairs/
pairs2/
pairs3/
pairs4/
pairs5/
pairs6/
tiny/
tiny2/
extracted/
extracted2/
extracted3/
x_*/
*.sbsar
*.sbsasm
*.sbs
*.png

# Derived caches and intermediate output
*.pkl
*.bak
__pycache__/
catalogue*.txt
catalogue.json
harvest2.txt
isa_census.txt
structmatch.txt
DISTINCT.txt

# Specimen directories are named one at a time above, and naming them one at a time is how
# `new_opengameart/` slipped through: 1,150 files, of which git would have added 252 --
# reference renders as .jpg and .gif, plus .xml and ReadMe.txt -- while its siblings
# new_acg/ and new_sbs/ were covered. The extension screen above stops .png, .sbsar, .sbs
# and .sbsasm; a materials pack ships far more than those.
#
# So the rules below are by TYPE, which is what actually distinguishes a specimen from
# source. Every tracked file in this repository is .py, .md, .json, .toml or a LICENCE, so
# these cannot hide a new tool, and they do not depend on where extraction put the files.
new_*/

# Reference renders and texture maps shipped alongside specimens
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.webp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.tga
*.dds
*.exr
*.hdr
*.psd
*.svg

# Meshes and presets that materials packs carry
*.obj
*.mtl
*.fbx
*.sbsprs

# Containers specimens arrive in
*.7z
*.zip

# macOS
.DS_Store
